IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cca-family-exclusion`

-- Casino Control Act 2006, ss 2, 157 to 168, 125 to 128, 195 -- family exclusion orders, worked cases.
--
-- Added on 11 October 2026 for REQ-0271 (Jun Hao scenario, event j081, 8 May 2046): Simone applies for a family exclusion order
-- against her brother Jun Hao, who gambles at the casino on paydays.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected results were written by hand from the
-- text. Facts the scenario does not give are ASSUMED and say so: Simone's age (44), that she is adversely affected, and that the
-- payday gambling has been repeated for six months.

§ `Fixtures`

-- ASSUMED: Simone is an adult, able to apply, and adversely affected by Jun Hao's gambling (s 159(1)(a) requires it).
`Simone, Jun Hao's sister` MEANS `Affected person` WITH
    `relationship to the respondent` IS `sibling`
    `adversely affected by the respondent's gambling` IS TRUE
    `likely to be adversely affected` IS TRUE
    `age in years` IS 44
    `able to make an application` IS TRUE

`a sister not yet affected but likely to be` MEANS `Affected person` WITH
    `relationship to the respondent` IS `sibling`
    `adversely affected by the respondent's gambling` IS FALSE
    `likely to be adversely affected` IS TRUE
    `age in years` IS 44
    `able to make an application` IS TRUE

`an affected cousin` MEANS `Affected person` WITH
    `relationship to the respondent` IS `cousin`
    `adversely affected by the respondent's gambling` IS TRUE
    `likely to be adversely affected` IS TRUE
    `age in years` IS 30
    `able to make an application` IS TRUE

`an affected 17-year-old half-sister` MEANS `Affected person` WITH
    `relationship to the respondent` IS `half-sibling`
    `adversely affected by the respondent's gambling` IS TRUE
    `likely to be adversely affected` IS TRUE
    `age in years` IS 17
    `able to make an application` IS TRUE

`an affected 15-year-old son` MEANS `Affected person` WITH
    `relationship to the respondent` IS `child`
    `adversely affected by the respondent's gambling` IS TRUE
    `likely to be adversely affected` IS TRUE
    `age in years` IS 15
    `able to make an application` IS TRUE

`an affected wife in hospital and unable to apply` MEANS `Affected person` WITH
    `relationship to the respondent` IS `spouse`
    `adversely affected by the respondent's gambling` IS TRUE
    `likely to be adversely affected` IS TRUE
    `age in years` IS 50
    `able to make an application` IS FALSE

-- ASSUMED: six months of payday gambling that leaves the family short; reason to think it will go on; notice served.
`Jun Hao gambling on paydays` MEANS `Family exclusion facts` WITH
    `gambled irresponsibly without regard to the family's needs and welfare` IS TRUE
    `months over which it was repeated` IS 6
    `particularly irresponsible over a shorter period` IS FALSE
    `reason to believe it will continue or recur` IS TRUE
    `the order is appropriate in the circumstances` IS TRUE
    `respondent given the s 158(2) notice and an opportunity to object` IS TRUE
    `absence order conditions in s 165C(1) met` IS FALSE
    `in the best interests of the respondent and the family` IS TRUE
    `the respondent consents` IS FALSE
    `frivolous, vexatious, without substance or hopeless` IS FALSE

`two paydays only` MEANS `Family exclusion facts` WITH
    `gambled irresponsibly without regard to the family's needs and welfare` IS TRUE
    `months over which it was repeated` IS 2
    `particularly irresponsible over a shorter period` IS FALSE
    `reason to believe it will continue or recur` IS TRUE
    `the order is appropriate in the circumstances` IS TRUE
